Subject: wined3d: select the vertex shader again when the pixel shader changes
Date: 2026-10-15
Applies to: CrossOver 26.3.0 Wine sources, after 0013
Files changed: dlls/wined3d/context_vk.c

For shader model 1-3, the vertex shader is compiled with a varying map built
from the pixel shader's inputs, which decides where each output is written.
The Vulkan backend only selected the vertex shader variant again when the
vertex shader or the vertex declaration changed, so after a pixel shader
change it kept writing to the previous pixel shader's inputs. The pixel shader
then read the wrong values, or inputs no vertex output wrote, which Metal
rejects ("Fragment input(s) ... not written by vertex shader"); each rejected
pipeline is a stall in BO1. A pixel shader change now selects the vertex
shader variant again.

Test: tools/d3d9-varying-test.c
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, like the Wine files it modifies.
---
--- a/dlls/wined3d/context_vk.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/context_vk.c
@@ -4053,9 +4053,13 @@
         context_vk->c.shader_update_mask |= (1u << WINED3D_SHADER_TYPE_PIXEL);
         context_vk->c.last_was_dual_source_blend = dual_source_blend;
     }
-    /* The vertex declaration selects which shader inputs are integers. */
+    /* The vertex declaration selects which shader inputs are integers, and
+     * for shader model 1-3 the pixel shader's inputs select where the vertex
+     * shader writes its outputs (the varying map), so a new pixel shader needs
+     * the matching vertex shader variant. */
     if (wined3d_context_is_graphics_state_dirty(&context_vk->c, STATE_SHADER(WINED3D_SHADER_TYPE_VERTEX))
-            || wined3d_context_is_graphics_state_dirty(&context_vk->c, STATE_VDECL))
+            || wined3d_context_is_graphics_state_dirty(&context_vk->c, STATE_VDECL)
+            || wined3d_context_is_graphics_state_dirty(&context_vk->c, STATE_SHADER(WINED3D_SHADER_TYPE_PIXEL)))
         context_vk->c.shader_update_mask |= (1u << WINED3D_SHADER_TYPE_VERTEX);
     if (wined3d_context_is_graphics_state_dirty(&context_vk->c, STATE_SHADER(WINED3D_SHADER_TYPE_GEOMETRY)))
         context_vk->c.shader_update_mask |= (1u << WINED3D_SHADER_TYPE_GEOMETRY);
